WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.490
February 1933.

2
00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:07.930
Two days after Hitler became Chancellor,
a young pastor speaks on German radio.

3
00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:11.950
His talk is about leaders who
turn themselves into idols.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.350
Before he finishes, the
broadcast is cut off.

5
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:18.060
The pastor is Dietrich Bonhoeffer.

6
00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:22.090
Twelve years later, the Nazi
state would execute him.

7
00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:25.270
The Bible tells Christians
to obey their rulers.

8
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:29.870
So when, if ever, must a
Christian resist the State?

9
00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:33.260
In this mission, you'll read
two Bible texts in tension,

10
00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:36.580
and follow a church's
struggle with the Nazi state.

11
00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:40.270
Then you'll weigh up whether Christians
should ever break the law for reasons

12
00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:41.620
of conscience.

13
00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:45.030
Your mission: find out how
Bonhoeffer answered this,

14
00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:47.310
in his writing and in his own life.
